    "blocks": [
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "This section shows how to use MockMvc on its own to test asynchronous request handling. If using MockMvc through the "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "WebTestClient"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "xref",
            "target": "testing/webtestclient.html"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", there is nothing special to do to make asynchronous requests work as the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "WebTestClient"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " automatically does what is described in this section."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Servlet asynchronous requests, "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "supported in Spring MVC"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "xref",
            "target": "web/webmvc/mvc-ann-async.html"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", work by exiting the Servlet container thread and allowing the application to compute the response asynchronously, after which an async dispatch is made to complete processing on a Servlet container thread."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "In Spring MVC Test, async requests can be tested by asserting the produced async value first, then manually performing the async dispatch, and finally verifying the response. Below is an example test for controller methods that return "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "DeferredResult"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Callable"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", or reactive type such as Reactor "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Mono"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ":"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "dlist",
            "id": null,
            "items": [
              {
                "description": {
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "context": "listing",
                      "id": null,
                      "inlines": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "// static import of MockMvcRequestBuilders.* and MockMvcResultMatchers.*\n\n@Test\nvoid test() throws Exception {\n       MvcResult mvcResult = this.mockMvc.perform(get(\"/path\"))\n               .andExpect(status().isOk()) "
                        },
                        {
                          "guard": null,
                          "icons": null,
                          "id": "CO1-1",
                          "kind": "callout",
                          "number": "1",
                          "src": "",
                          "xml": false
                        },
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "\n               .andExpect(request().asyncStarted()) "
                        },
                        {
                          "guard": null,
                          "icons": null,
                          "id": "CO1-2",
                          "kind": "callout",
                          "number": "2",
                          "src": "",
                          "xml": false
                        },
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "\n               .andExpect(request().asyncResult(\"body\")) "
                        },
                        {
                          "guard": null,
                          "icons": null,
                          "id": "CO1-3",
                          "kind": "callout",
                          "number": "3",
                          "src": "",
                          "xml": false
                        },
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "\n               .andReturn();\n\n       this.mockMvc.perform(asyncDispatch(mvcResult)) "
                        },
                        {
                          "guard": null,
                          "icons": null,
                          "id": "CO1-4",
                          "kind": "callout",
                          "number": "4",
                          "src": "",
                          "xml": false
                        },
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "\n               .andExpect(status().isOk()) "
                        },
                        {
                          "guard": null,
                          "icons": null,
                          "id": "CO1-5",
                          "kind": "callout",
                          "number": "5",
                          "src": "",
                          "xml": false
                        },
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "\n               .andExpect(content().string(\"body\"));\n   }"
                        }
                      ],
                      "language": "java",
                      "roles": [],
                      "title": null
                    },
